; tap2sna.py file for Cyberun. Run
;
;   $ tap2sna.py @cyberun.t2s
;
; to create a Z80 snapshot.

https://zxaaa.net/DENIED/Cyberun%20(1985)(Ultimate%20Play%20The%20Game).tzx
Cyberun.z80

--sim-load-config accelerator=speedlock

; The BASIC loader loads a helper block to $6000 (it copies the loading screen
; to $4000 and a stub to $5B80) and then loads the encrypted game to $5E80.
; The stub at $5B80 (LD SP,$FE00; DI; CALL $FC00; LD HL,$FA00; XOR A;
; LD BC,$9E00; RRD loop; JP $5C80) moves the game down to $5C80 and decrypts
; it nibble by nibble with RRD. The simulation runs all of that, so stopping at
; the start address leaves the decrypted game at its real addresses with
; nothing else to do here.
--start 23680
